Subject: [PATCH 09/11] d3d10umd, yttrium: compute, constant-buffer and resource-coherence fixes

- Accept cube and cube-array resources behind 2D-array SRVs and
  RWTexture2DArray UAVs, and initialise every mip and layer of depth arrays
  (F21-F22).
- Resource waits flush the recording command batch and add a buffer-to-host
  barrier, so CPU reads of GPU-written buffers see the producer (F38).
- Ordered CPU uploads into mapped buffers snapshot pure vertex/index buffers
  per draw and wait for earlier GPU reads before overwriting (staged-draw-0212,
  Heaven D3D9 menu).
- Compute shaders may sample buffer SRVs through uniform texel buffers (F33).
- Constant buffers written by the GPU are read back before CPU constant
  collection, and compute constants stay in their GPU buffer (F224-F229).
- DispatchIndirect runs natively through vkCmdDispatchIndirect with argument
  validation and barriers, instead of a CPU readback stall (F230-F231).

Prior art: F21, F22, F33, F38, F224-F231, staged-draw-0212 (R/NATIVE-WDDM20.md; V/EXPERIMENTS.md).
Origin: codex working tree R/mesa (git diff 374c3022), re-exported by
vmlab-win3d build/mesa; see build/mesa/README.md.
